  "summary": "Malicious code in tramvai-tinkoff-module-legacy-popup (npm)",
  "details": "The package auto-loads setup.js on require(), which fingerprints the host OS and architecture, then downloads a platform-specific binary payload from Cloudflare Workers C2 infrastructure (oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev) via HTTPS GET to paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, or /pkg/package.exe. If HTTPS fails, it falls back to DNS TXT-based chunked download via the domain tin[.]dl[.]well1[.]site. The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003crandom\u003e (or %TEMP%\\dotnet_diag_\u003crandom\u003e.exe on Windows) and executed as a detached background process. The package has no repository, no README, and exports a dummy class — the entire purpose is to deliver and execute a remote binary payload.",
